{
    "_documentation": "Six-lever rotary hexapod starting point. Copy next to the executable as rig.json (or paste axes into the web editor) and adjust per leg. Rotary convention: the engineering unit is DEGREES at the lever shaft -- strokeMm = arc travel in degrees, speeds in deg/s, ballscrewPitch pinned to 360. Keys omitted here fall back to compiled-in defaults (see resources/rig.reference.json and Docs/CONFIG_REFERENCE.md). Walkthrough: Docs/HEXAPOD_SETUP.md.",
    "configVersion": 2,
    "numDrives": 6,
    "global": {
        "conditioningMode": "bypass",
        "requireUserFaultReset": false
    },
    "_axes_notes": "slaveIndex = chain order. invertDir alternates for mirrored leg pairs as a starting point -- VERIFY per leg: home one axis at a time (Commissioning Tests panel) and flip invertDir on any leg that searches toward the wrong end. followingErrorWindowMm is degrees on a lever and must stay within the arc (enforced). parkMode center: a lever has no gravity-defined rest.",
